t.textos.gilgamesh.pasajes.0.texto:
He who has tasted (the heart of) all things, let him [teach] it to the nation;
[he who] possesses all knowledge, let him [instruct] all the people with it;
[he will impart his wisdom (?)] and (so) they will [share] it together.
[Gilgamesh (?)], he was [master] of wisdom, with [knowledge of all things];
it was he who discovered the hidden secret […],
(yes), he handed down the tradition of (the things) before the flood;
he went on a long journey, (weary) and [worn out by his toil (?)],
he [engraved] on a tablet of stone all his travail.
Of Uruk, the high-walled,
he built the ramparts, (and) he made firm the foundation.
